The doubly charmed baryons $\Xi_{cc}$ and $\Omega_{cc}$ are studied using the quark model, specifically the quark pair model, to determine their semileptonic transition form factors. The form factors are calculated for various transitions, including $\Xi_{cc}^{++} 	o \Xi_{c}^{+} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}$, $\Xi_{cc}^{++} 	o \Lambda_{c}^{+} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}$, $\Omega_{cc}^{+} 	o \Xi_{c}^{0} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}$, and $\Omega_{cc}^{+} 	o \Lambda_{c}^{+} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}$. The form factors are then used to predict the branching ratios of these transitions, which are found to be in the range of $10^{-3}$ to $10^{-4}$. The results are compared with other theoretical models, and the predictions are found to be in good agreement with the lattice QCD calculations. The predictions can be tested experimentally by the LHCb and Belle II experiments.
